<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1d32ecce8d2d57fab5a5f5dad1c1bdcea59ce189e78700cf085b45060252fb1</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1" /><summary type="html">Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.</summary></entry><entry><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75eb937a1f1117856993f7fdd435e4acadcc86ab7a246882d0a037d55b75e48c</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:45:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd" /><summary type="html">Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa12b7441f4df1b59bb3a7d4739682df6eaaa5e39b86f524c1d3a431cc7488d0</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Jubilation and pain': German far right marches to victory in key state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37c4359633fbee2c6ef5e3634c5bc41b9b8399d6b5b7447acda675e7c3d9db13</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:05:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 7: The far right marches to victory in a German state election: what does this mean for the future of Germany and Europe at large? Also: the Daily Telegraph publishes an exclusive interview with the sons of former Pakistani PM Imran Khan about his imprisonment conditions in Pakistan. Plus the US Open descends into chaos after influencers, weed and disruptions stir controversy.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks to dismiss Nicaragua's Gaza genocide case at top UN court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6860c4a98adcbb3563404bce6bee2667f7bc91c5c480941a80225d1987e6734c</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:14:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court" /><summary type="html">Germany is set to ask the International Court of Justice on Monday to dismiss a case accusing Berlin of "facilitating genocide" in Gaza by supporting Israel after the deadly October 7, 2023 attacks by Hamas militants. The details of the case, filed by Nicaragua in 2024, have not yet been made public.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of mourners gather in Belgrade for war criminal Mladic's funeral</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61c59f63fe9f4797cb9cfb8022866c51eb0edf6f04b05a2edd89355109485c1b</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T08:08:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-thousands-of-mourners-gather-in-belgrade-for-war-criminal-mladic-s-funeral" /><summary type="html">Thousands of mourners on Monday gathered at a church in Belgrade to view the body of Ratko Mladic, who died in The Hague, Netherlands, on August 27 while serving a life sentence for genocide, war crimes and crimes against humanity. The European Union has heavily criticised the event, and Marta Kos, the bloc's enlargement commissioner, cancelled an upcoming visit to Serbia in protest.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Germany’s Merz 'deeply shocked' by far-right AfD's historic electoral victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cb636323073432f074b21b0033bcb42cdba4836a4aedb2971ef0f9c0bdf7d58</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T06:30:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-live-europe-reacts-to-germany-far-right-afd-worrying-electoral-victory" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz told the press on Monday that he was "deeply shocked" by the far-right AfD's historic victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election a day earlier. The AfD is labelled a "right-wing extremist" group by Germany's domestic intelligence agency, and some of its staff are former members of a since-banned neo-Nazi organisation. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz vows to stick with reforms despite election drubbing by far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51443c546e12a7c49342a36a6a572056c2ed876228cd0568e883f31c8ffbbfe0</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T05:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-s-merz-shocked-by-far-right-state-win-but-vows-to-stay-course" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Monday vowed to press ahead with his reform agenda despite a blistering election defeat for his centre-right CDU in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right AfD won almost 44 percent of the vote. Merz called the result his party’s worst defeat in decades.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys bring ‘more effective’ Ukraine peace proposals to Kyiv, official says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8270d94f6332a3d7af07c5ad6f559b0ff2b14d34437f4447cc846e513fd898fb</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:31:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv--37419914ba3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv" /><summary type="html">US envoys brought new, “more effective” proposals to Kyiv aimed at ending the war with Russia, a senior Ukrainian presidential official said on Sunday. President Volodymyr Zelensky and US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner described talks positively but announced no breakthrough, as Zelensky warned fighting could continue into winter.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU to boost Greenland investment amid Trump annexation claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5633faefd886062bd1cfd7cc35fd0f5c72e960eaf6079579b9d5bffce3525c1a</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T00:27:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation--2b5a527b0c9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen is expected to announce increased EU investment in Greenland on Monday, including in critical minerals, satellite communications and renewable energy. Her two-day visit signals support for Greenland and Denmark amid US President Donald Trump’s push for American control of the Arctic territory.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Ready to talk': German far right celebrates victory in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8984badb6b30e39499d035c941fb5c2744e47203f8cc34be34eca50736d4ee64</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T17:32:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory--e252fd4fc28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory" /><summary type="html">"Everything is possible" was the campaign slogan of the Alternative for Germany (AfD) in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right party has won a landslide election victory, although they appear short of a majority in the state parliament. Ulrich Siegmund, who is in pole position to become the state leader, knows he has history in his grasp. We get reaction from CSU MP Tobias Winkler.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s far-right AfD wins big in key state election but falls short of majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:422bd17db10e9f2725ed10e1802ffad4caf58e5f194e6218471be631eefbfc86</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T16:15:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest--ba93eb6e2f1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest" /><summary type="html">Germany’s far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party headed towards a landslide victory in state ​elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in its bid to form the country's first far-right state government since World War II. However, final results showed AfD falling three seats short of an absolute majority, with 39 lawmakers in an 83-member parliament.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Nepal rescue operations, World Nomad Games and Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e7cfe1963ca27fe2a39b8dc5ac64f6c92a01d50b418594df5553def171f28f</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T14:21:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv--d0868f737f26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">From the desperate search for workers trapped in the hydropower tunnels buried by the catastrophic flooding in Nepal to crowds of women mourning the victims of a US bombardment of a wedding in southern Iran, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'A bad sign': US envoys head to Kyiv after three-hour talks with Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d8f7b7e69ecbbfaab646b241ee6970c850daf5517a871dcac6f2efd1b50a74e</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T06:18:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-bad-sign-us-envoys-head-to-kyiv-after-three-hour-talks-with-putin--ef402e9abb2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-bad-sign-us-envoys-head-to-kyiv-after-three-hour-talks-with-putin" /><summary type="html">As US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner head to Kyiv following what the White House described as "substantive" talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin, FRANCE 24 correspondent Gulliver Cragg talks about what he describes as a climate of scepticism in Ukraine that these latest negotiations could bring a long-awaited breakthrough.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD eyes historic state victory in Saxony-Anhalt election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:548c5efe933a6ab0b29b218538aa4053083b13e906d6aaeed878929a43767805</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:52:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-eyes-historic-state-victory-in-saxony-anhalt-election--d84eb1b6b427.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-eyes-historic-state-victory-in-saxony-anhalt-election" /><summary type="html">Germany's anti-immigrant Alternative for Germany party is aiming to become the first far-right party to take power at a state level since World War II as voters in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt head to the polls Sunday. However, a failure to secure an absolute majority may see the politically isolated party struggle to form a government.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>After meeting with US envoys in Kyiv, Zelensky says war likely to ‘continue in winter’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c06d4b512dca6bdd1abec711aa1383377d02b758ba785c4ff46ae15495a44ae</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T04:57:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-live-trump-s-envoys-head-to-ukraine-after-substantive-talks-with-putin--f41091ccbfca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-live-trump-s-envoys-head-to-ukraine-after-substantive-talks-with-putin" /><summary type="html">Although Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky described talks with US special envoy Steve Witkoff and Donald Trump’s son-in-law Jared Kushner as “substantial”, he warned that the war with Russia was likely to continue this winter. The US envoys arrived in Kyiv for their first official visit on Sunday, a day after meeting Russia’s President Vladimir Putin in Moscow. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Witkoff: Putin's messenger?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5708bcb016af62bb356331297a8077c6e7ac1489173a9772d13a2bad7620e097</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T18:02:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260905-witkoff-putin-s-messenger--1b668b4d5419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260905-witkoff-putin-s-messenger" /><summary type="html">What did Steve Witkoff know about Russia when he was first sent to see President Vladimir Putin in February of last year?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Two senior Reform UK officials resign as Farage faces fresh foreign donations scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1499cb3f52c23f24c82e418db6cd74431098db4da58f14f28d18bbfef8014714</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:30:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-two-senior-reform-uk-officials-resign-as-farage-faces-fresh-foreign-donations-scandal--c43eb44d3d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-two-senior-reform-uk-officials-resign-as-farage-faces-fresh-foreign-donations-scandal" /><summary type="html">Two senior officials from the hard-right Reform UK party stepped down Friday following a hidden-camera investigation that appeared to show them soliciting substantial foreign funding for party-commissioned opinion polls and a potential £500,000 donation from a US donor – banned under UK law.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Putin orders 72-hour halt in strikes on Kyiv as Trump envoys arrive in Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a0496d902d05df49a8a03a4111f061b07c85df125e1e5e7a1d4ae0c1bfd64bf</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T02:37:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-and-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-the-war--2b81279000c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-and-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-the-war" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Saturday ordered a 72-hour pause in strikes on Kyiv as US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrived in Moscow. The visit is part of renewed efforts to end the war in Ukraine, and the two men are set to travel to Kyiv on Sunday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>German power grid sabotage attack linked to ‘climate extremism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:694da36134db6b1893df99034dcee01c332669bbc96630c858ae40db1bbabed8</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:40:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism--b5a9f0391572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt on Friday said the evidence in a recent spate of sabotage attacks on power grids across the country points to a militant climate activist.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s ‘Most Dangerous Man’: PR gift for the AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3c74bd712e4eaf51604d024777b88e83df5ab6d49ec4095d3883b8b18725dff</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:31:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd--f852f5df9336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd" /><summary type="html">The Ukrainian capital was hit by Russia’s most intense wave of air attacks on Kyiv, reportedly in four years, with Reuters describing air raid sirens, drones, cruise and ballistic missiles exhausting Ukraine’s defence system, with 12 people killed and the Ukrainian foreign minister making a direct appeal to Western allies for more Patriot interceptor missiles.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>'Italian opposition fragmented: No alternative leader, no other possible leader than Giorgia Meloni'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f52e920a61688b156df64f7d2b9ba87c64e65f87108272a873450f9008978ce</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-m--1c36e6864261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-meloni-1" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Political analyst Lorenzo Pregliasco, co-founder of polling agency YouTrend and adjunct professor at the University of Bologna. He argues that Giorgia Meloni’s unusual longevity in office is best understood not simply as a record of political strength, but as the product of a carefully calibrated governing strategy. Meloni has maintained stability partly by avoiding structural reforms disruptive enough to mobilize multiple constituencies against her at once. Her dominance within Fratelli d’Italia, the absence of a credible alternative leader, and a fragmented opposition have reinforced that advantage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider, the ideologist behind the AFD’s plans in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5563bd0ce66277997a997d82fe5a4b99581970c5968a014541e30aa42e4c28f</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt--220beb71b19c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt" /><summary type="html">The far-right German political party Alternative for Germany could win a historical victory in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt in key elections this Sunday. The party’s agenda is more radical than ever and inspired by the proposals of an influential ideologist in the region: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France announces €1 billion aid for farmers after climate-hit summer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aae5509176d003486243db340befada2c14262457cd0701a370c2a545dfb98c</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:12:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-_1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer--e6ed56d5d705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-%E2%82%AC1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer" /><summary type="html">France has recorded its hottest summer on record this year as the country battled heatwaves, drought and massive wildfires. The extreme weather has continued into September, with France's national weather service placing five departments on orange alert for several days. Temperatures are expected to reach 40°C in some areas. France's agriculture minister also announced a plan to unlock over 1 billion euros in aid to the agriculture sector, which has been severely affected by the extreme weather.</summary></entry><entry><title>Strengthening Africa is an investment in Europe's future: EU Commissioner Jozef Sikela</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32194e8b0120cca153d1a8bd90cee31590b6b91472914200eecffa17fb8c08d7</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:03:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-strengthening-africa-is-an-investment-in-europe-s-future-eu-commissioner-jozef-sikela--f05b28eefbd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-strengthening-africa-is-an-investment-in-europe-s-future-eu-commissioner-jozef-sikela" /><summary type="html">Are great-power politics back, at the expense of smaller countries? In an age of strongmen, is multilateralism in retreat? Not according to Jozef Sikela. The EU Commissioner in charge of International Partnerships insists that traditional multilateralism is alive and well, especially in the EU's approach to Africa and to the Arctic. We sat down with him for an interview at the European Commission in Brussels.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone strikes Ukraine security service HQ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d65280cab02168df0a81890b5541fdfeebf966aa622658c9ec1b0138413d8dd6</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:59:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says--9847636126d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone struck the headquarters of Ukraine's SBU security services in Kyiv on Friday afternoon, said Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, injuring five people. The attack followed a series of deadly overnight strikes across Ukraine, including the southern Odesa region.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Meloni celebrates milestone as Italy's longest-lasting government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fe7c7e1d9b0c960cc55550cfe35b9382bfe2c60df064459b3f1b5e87de00670</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:50:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-meloni-celebrates-milestone-as-italy-s-longest-lasting-government--f397a1fc9a52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-meloni-celebrates-milestone-as-italy-s-longest-lasting-government" /><summary type="html">Italy's Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni is celebrating a milestone: her hard-right government is now the longest-lasting in the country's post war history. In a country known for its political instability, it's a notable record. But considerable challenges remain for Italy's first female prime minister, ahead of elections next year. FRANCE 24's Italy correspondent Seema Gupta reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Struggling to make its voice heard: Can the EU forge a true foreign policy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:415164a10f4996f1b126220b8e60152ec1cc9074747d7043c87a95b1f360d11e</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:42:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-struggling-to-make-its-voice-heard-can-the-eu-forge-a-true-foreign-policy--d3fdfae86cb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-struggling-to-make-its-voice-heard-can-the-eu-forge-a-true-foreign-policy" /><summary type="html">"Who do I call if I want to speak to Europe?" The famous quote attributed to Henry Kissinger still resonates today. There is in fact a Mrs Europe on the world stage: Kaja Kallas, the EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy. She is actually the sixth high representative. But ever since that post was created, rivalries between different centres of power have diluted the EU's ability to speak with one voice. We saw that recently with tensions over who should represent the EU in any potential talks with Russia.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Strength of Meloni less linked to policy, more about her party's dominance within govt coalition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fd951450b5e347130668aa335468ceb6a45040063ad162cf910a0d16b80ac12</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:24:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/strength-of-meloni-less-linked-to-policy-more-about-her-party-s-dominance-within-govt-coalition--987072e3c262.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/strength-of-meloni-less-linked-to-policy-more-about-her-party-s-dominance-within-govt-coalition" /><summary type="html">William Hilderbrandt is pleased to welcome Dr. Giulia Sandri, Associate researcher at the Free University of Brussels. Meloni has benefited from something historically scarce in Italian politics: longevity. Four years of governmental stability have allowed her to accumulate diplomatic relationships, strengthening Italy’s position within Europe and giving Rome greater visibility internationally. Yet Sandri argues that this political success sits alongside a much less decisive domestic record. Improvements in employment and fiscal credibility coexist with weak growth, stagnant wages, declining purchasing power and persistent structural problems in healthcare, education, demographics and public administration.</summary></entry><entry><title>What does acquittal in the Daphne Caruana Galizia case mean for journalists?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ca1a3a71e050b8b501a44f61bfb37a5ca4f028e72b16ad8a2cbe40689cea1f4</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:07:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260904-what-does-acquittal-in-the-daphne-caruana-galizia-case-mean-for-journalists--f23eee59cc84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260904-what-does-acquittal-in-the-daphne-caruana-galizia-case-mean-for-journalists" /><summary type="html">This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at the murder of anti-corruption journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Press freedom groups are furious after Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech was acquitted of involvement. Caruana Galizia was an outspoken critic of the government and described as a "one-woman WikiLeaks". She was killed by a car bomb in 2017 and speculation followed that influential figures may have been involved. Our guest is the Times of Malta Editor-in-Chief, Herman Grech.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry></feed>
